<Item XName="ReadMe" UserName="ReadMe" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;AM_to_PM_RF_model_LTE&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;This&amp;nbsp;example workspace&amp;nbsp;demonstrates AM-to-PM parameters&amp;nbsp;in the nonlinear RFAMP model. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;The workspace uses&amp;nbsp;a 2505 MHz LTE Uplink signal as a stimulus.&amp;nbsp;Because of this, you will need licenses for the W1719 RF System and W1910 LTE&amp;nbsp;Library&amp;nbsp;to run the simulation as&amp;nbsp;shown. Otherwise, you can replace the source signal with another desired signal.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;The device-under-test is a&amp;nbsp;RFAMP model in the &quot;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0000ff&gt;RF_PA_with_AM_PM&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&quot; schematic with the following parameters:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;Gain = 17 dB&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;OP1dB = +25 dBm&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;OPSAT = +28 dBm&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;AMtoPM = +2.1 degrees/dB&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;PwrAMtoPM = (the output power level at which the slope is specified) =&amp;nbsp;+24.5 dBm&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;Several simple measurements are presented here, using native SystemVue post-processing capabilities. Enabling the Keysight 89600B VSA sink on the schematic allows demodulation of the signal using its LTE personality, including spectrum, constellation, EVM, AM/AM and AM/PM measurements. There is excellent agreement between the SystemVue calculations and the displayed measurements on the 89600B VSA.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;Model Validation&amp;nbsp;- Measurements &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0000ff&gt;Spectrum Measurements&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; is captured using the &lt;EM&gt;SpectrumAnalyzer&lt;/EM&gt; sink. This is used to quickly assess ACLR and spectral re-growth, for spec pre-compliance.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0000ff&gt;CCDF_Measurements&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; shows the percentage of time (y-axis) that the instantaneous LTE signal envelope spends above the average power level (x-axis).&amp;nbsp;The &quot;crest factor&quot; of the signal is essentially the dB value of the x-axis intercept, and shows the amplitude of the highest signal peaks normalized to the RMS signal power.&amp;nbsp;A second CCDF trace is a reference trace of white gaussian noise, for comparison.&amp;nbsp;A CCDF curve that abruptly falls to a low value shows lower power handling, or clipping.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;The &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0000ff&gt;AMtoAM_and_AMtoPM&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;graph shows the normalized power gain and output phase of the LTE signal (vs. input power level) on a point-by-point basis for the complex-valued modulated carrier envelope.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;When these traces are flat lines, the DUT is operating in a very linear region.&amp;nbsp; (no change from nominal, regardless of time or amplitude)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;When these traces curve upward or downward vs. power, then DUT is showing some nonlinearity.&amp;nbsp;This&amp;nbsp;level of simulation modeling is common, and is&amp;nbsp;considered a&amp;nbsp;&quot;Level 1&quot; model.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;When the traces spread into a statistical distribution, then the DUT is&amp;nbsp;demonstrating that some output values depend on the previous signal history in addition to the absolute power levels.&amp;nbsp;These are so-called &quot;baseband memory effects&quot;, which are possible with Level 3 Models.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#800080 size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;Incidentally, note that there is no explicit sweep taking place; we use the fact that the time domain simulation captures the output signal at many levels of the input signal ranging from zero to maximum level, and these data are&amp;nbsp;used to generate the statistical scatter plots vs. input power level. This is a cool trick!&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=#800080 size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;EXERCISES&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Adjust the LTE source power level&lt;/STRONG&gt; using the tuning slider.&amp;nbsp;Change the value&amp;nbsp;from the minimum to the maximum power levels, and note the changes to the output&amp;nbsp;traces.&amp;nbsp; Note the observed power levels and Crest Factors right on the schematic.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;(optional ) Use the 89600 VSA software for deeper post-processing.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;If you have access to the Keysight 89600B VSA software (release 11 or later with its LTE options), activate the VSA measurement sink and re-simulate.&amp;nbsp;(It takes several seconds the first time it runs).&amp;nbsp; The VSA gives you further measurement ability on the LTE signals, such as&amp;nbsp;EVM for each of the LTE data and control sub-signals; integrated bandwidth power measurements to measure ACLR, and many more capabilities.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;U&gt;User Tip&lt;/U&gt;:&amp;nbsp; After you have simulated into the VSA and observe the results, you can &quot;STOP&quot; the SystemVue simulation, but don&apos;t close the VSA; this saves time when you next re-simulate.&amp;nbsp;Slide the slider to a new power level while the&amp;nbsp;simulation is running and see the effect on the signals. The convenience of this method reduces the amount of time you spend&amp;nbsp;doing verification.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;SUMMARY&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;In this example, the simulations&amp;nbsp;only take a few&amp;nbsp;seconds, yet are fairly realistic modulated PA results.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;This level of verification would be nearly impossible for an analog&amp;nbsp;IC with thousands of transistors using transient Spice and primitive signal sources.&amp;nbsp;A few key capabilities make this easy:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;The envelope simulation mode&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;A&amp;nbsp;fast dataflow simulation backplane in SystemVue, with a full LTE reference library and native&amp;nbsp;AM-to-PM model integration&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;The SystemVue environment to bridge the&amp;nbsp;design flow gap between&amp;nbsp;Architecture, Implementation, Verification, and Test &amp;amp; Measurement.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;Finally, for a more realistic model, consider either generating an X-parameter model, a Fast Circuit Envelope model from GoldenGate, or co-simulating with the DUT schematic in ADS or GoldenGate.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;The exact same tools&amp;nbsp;and signals used here can&amp;nbsp;also be used to generate signals after tape-out to measure the real hardware transceiver with Keysight signal sources and analyzers.&amp;nbsp; This allows you&amp;nbsp;to compare the results directly (&quot;apples to apples&quot;), and to feed back measurements into the architecture process to close your modeling loop.&amp;nbsp; Bring your hardware measurements back into SystemVue, and be using real waveforms for your next design start!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Segoe UI&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
